      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if instead of passing jiffies on the lock and zero on the unlock (which is sort of subtle/unintuitive semantics for the interface - ie: calling start-time at the end) it would be more clear to have an _acquire() function and a _release() function? Then the vh implementation itself can decide if it wants to sample jiffies or not.\n\nThoughts?\n\nAdditionally some of the locking primitives are getting really busy with tracepoints (see rwsems for a good example). Are there any existing tracepoints that could be re-used instead of adding new ones?",
